    "lawSection": "Commissions",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6990\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to create a temporary New York state War of 1812 200th\nanniversary commemoration commission to promote the 200th anniversary\nof the War of 1812\n\n\n PURPOSE OF GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nTo create a temporary commission to commemorate the 200th anniversary\nof the War of 1812.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1. Legislative Findings\n\nSection 2. Creates the commissions; defines terms.\n\nSection 3. Composition of commission\n\nSection 4. Powers and duties of the commission.\n\nSection 5. Assistance to the commission.\n\nSection 6. Commission authorized to carry out its duties.\n\nSection 7. Commission will be repealed on December 31, 2015.\n\nSection 8. Effective Date\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nNew York State played a key role in War of 1812.  Celebrating this\nmilestone gives New Yorkers the opportunity to appreciate and reflect\non our rich history. During the years 2012-2015, New York State will\nmark, within its borders, the 200th anniversary of the great battles\nof the War of 1812. New York State, its counties, cities, towns and\nvillages may profit, both culturally and economically, from the\nbenefits of a statewide commission to help organize, promote and fully\nimplement a major commemoration of the 200th Anniversary of the War of\n1812. By promoting New York State's magnificent history, we can make,\nNew York the ultimate heritage tourism destination for the years\n2012-2015.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nS.5603C: 2009 Vetoed\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n Not applicable.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
