    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6990B\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act to create a temporary New York state War of 1812 200th anniver-\nsary commemoration commission to promote the 200th anniversary of the\nWar of 1812\n\nPURPOSE OF GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo create a temporary commission to commemorate the 200th anniversary of\nthe War of 1812.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection 1. Legislative Findings\n\nSection 2. Creates the commissions; defines terms.\n\nSection 3. Composition of commission\n\nSection 4. Powers and duties of the commission.\n\nSection 5. Assistance to the commission.\n\nSection 6. Commission authorized to carry out its duties.\n\nSection 7. Commission will be repealed on December 31, 2015.\n\nSection 8. Effective Date\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nNew York State played a key role in the War of 1812. Celebrating this\nmilestone gives New Yorkers the opportunity to appreciate and reflect on\nour rich history. During the years 2012-2015, New York State will mark,\nwithin its borders, the 200th anniversary of the great battles of the\nWar of 1812. New York State, its counties, cities, towns and villages\nmay profit, both culturally and economically, from the benefits of a\nstatewide commission to help organize, promote and fully implement a\nmajor commemoration of the 200th Anniversary of the War of 1812. By\npromoting New York State's magnificent history, we can make, New York\nthe ultimate heritage tourism destination for the years 2012-2015.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nS.5603C: 2009 Vetoed\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNot applicable.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
